            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Geometric Twins"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.088,
            0.748,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Corresponding Sides: AB and XY, BC and YZ, AC and XZ"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.113,
            0.777,
            0.134
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) Corresponding Angles: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { X } , \\angle \\mathrm { B }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { Y } , \\angle \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { Z }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.144,
            0.847,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To capture this relation that exists when two triangles are congruent, their congruence is written as follows:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.188,
            0.609,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.389,
                0.188,
                0.609,
                0.327
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.338,
            0.449,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By writing this, we mean that:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.363,
            0.846,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the first vertex in the name of ΔABC corresponds to the first vertex in the name of ΔXYZ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.405,
            0.846,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the second vertex in the name of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " corresponds to the second vertex in the name of ΔXYZ, and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.447,
            0.839,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• similarly with the third vertices in the names of ΔABC and ΔXYZ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.47,
            0.846,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By this convention, it is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "incorrect",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to write for these two triangles that ΔACB ≅ ΔXYZ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.513,
            0.608,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "However, another correct way of saying it is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.533,
            0.579,
            0.552
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\Delta  ACB  \\cong \\Delta  XZY."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.562,
            0.847,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you identify a pair of congruent triangles below? Why are they congruent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.602,
            0.67,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.326,
                0.602,
                0.67,
                0.761
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.773,
            0.774,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and ΔCDB. Since ABCD is a rectangle, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.457,
            0.793,
            0.541,
            0.811
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{AB} = \\mathrm{CD}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.456,
            0.813,
            0.542,
            0.83
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{AD} = \\mathrm{CB}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.831,
            0.847,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the remaining sides of ΔABD and ΔCDB have the same length then the SSS condition is satisfied, confirming the congruence of the two triangles. Is this the case?"
            }
          ]
        },
